      "doctor_question": "Hello, I’m glad you came in. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S001",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, hi. Thanks. Um, well, I guess what brings me in is that I just keep making these really dumb mistakes at work. I supervise a sales team, and I have to do all these reports, and lately I just keep copying the wrong numbers from the team dashboard. \n\nWhich, honestly, the dashboard is a total mess right now. We got this new software last month because the regional director went to some tech conference down in Austin and got totally sold on it. I mean, Austin's great, the barbecue is amazing down there—I went for a buddy's bachelor party a few years ago and we ate at this place that had a line around the block—but this software they bought is just terrible. The interface makes no sense. \n\nBut anyway, yeah, the numbers. I'll put the wrong ones in, or I'll completely miss a line in a procedure I was supposed to check. And the crazy thing is, I swear I look it over. I'll sit there, double-check it, think I went over the whole thing perfectly, and then my boss will point out I skipped a whole section. It's just getting really embarrassing.",
