      "doctor_question": "Did you have similar problems with inattention or careless mistakes when you were a child, before age 12?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh man, yeah. I was totally like this as a kid too. Actually, my mom still brings it up. She kept all these old teacher notes from elementary school in this big plastic tub in her basement. Which, by the way, her basement flooded last spring because the sump pump failed, and she had to throw out half her stuff. I told her to get a backup battery for it years ago, but you know how it is, nobody listens until there's a foot of water ruining all your old yearbooks and stuff. \n\nBut anyway, yeah, she managed to save some of those teacher notes, and they all basically said the exact same thing. That I rushed through my work, lost my homework constantly, talked out of turn... oh, and that I couldn't stay seated without being reminded. Like, I was always popping up out of my chair. So yeah, I guess it's been happening for a long time.",
